  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nLet $A_1, G_1, H_1$ denote the arithmetic, geometric and harmonic means respectively, of two distinct positive numbers. For $n \\geq 2$, let $A_{n-1}$ and $H_{n-1}$ has arithmetic, geometric and harmonic means as $A_n, G_n, H_n$, respectively.<strong>Question:</strong>\nWhich one of the following statements is correct?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "y7QbW",
      "text": "\n$G_1>G_2>G_3>\\ldots$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PnRmU",
      "text": "\n$G_1 < G_2 < G_3 < \\ldots$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Dp9r2",
      "text": "\n$G_1=G_2=G_3=\\ldots$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "9jpZq",
      "text": "\n$G_1 < G_3 < G_5 < \\ldots$ and $G_2>G_4>G_6>\\ldots$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$A_1=\\frac{a+b}{2}, G_1=\\sqrt{a b}$ and $H_1=\\frac{2 a b}{a+b}$ $\\begin{aligned} A_n=\\frac{A_{n-1}+H_{n-1}}{2}, G_n & =\\sqrt{A_{n-1} H_{n-1}}, \\\\ H_n & =\\frac{2 A_{n-1} H_{n-1}}{A_{n-1}+H_{n-1}}\\end{aligned}$\nClearly, $\\quad G_1=G_2=G_3=\\ldots=\\sqrt{a b}$.",
    "image": null
  },
